#: g7-guidance.json
msgctxt "g7-guidance.json:review.g7-slp-data-flow.how"
msgid "Write down how data moves through the system: where an input comes from, what the model receives, and where its output goes. Confirm the description matches how the system is actually deployed."
msgstr ""

#: g7-guidance.json
msgctxt "g7-guidance.json:review.g7-slp-data-usage.how"
msgid "State what the system does with the data it receives — whether it is stored, passed to another component, or used for further training. Check this against the privacy notice you publish."
msgstr ""

#: g7-guidance.json
msgctxt "g7-guidance.json:review.g7-slp-io.how"
msgid "Describe the input and output the system accepts and produces — formats, size limits, and anything it refuses. A person confirms this because a model card lists modalities, not the system's actual interface."
msgstr ""

#: g7-guidance.json
msgctxt "g7-guidance.json:review.g7-slp-app-area.how"
msgid "State the field the system is intended for and the uses that are out of scope. This is a decision, not a fact a tool can read, and regulators ask for it directly."
msgstr ""

#: g7-guidance.json
msgctxt "g7-guidance.json:review.g7-ds-statistics.how"
msgid "Give the size and shape of the training data — record counts, class balance, and any known skew. These numbers explain the model's limits, so state them even when they are unflattering."
msgstr ""

#: g7-guidance.json
msgctxt "g7-guidance.json:review.g7-ds-sensitivity.how"
msgid "Judge whether the training data holds personal information or third-party copyrighted work, and record what you filtered out and how. Where the answer is unclear, take it to your privacy and legal contacts before release."
msgstr ""

#: g7-guidance.json
msgctxt "g7-guidance.json:review.g7-sec-controls.how"
msgid "List the controls that protect the model and its data — who can reach the weights, how the training environment is isolated, how artefacts are signed. These live in your operations, not in the SBOM."
msgstr ""

#: g7-guidance.json
msgctxt "g7-guidance.json:review.g7-sec-compliance.how"
msgid "Name the security standard or internal policy this model was built under, and who signed off. Point at the assessment record rather than restating it here."
msgstr ""

#: g7-guidance.json
msgctxt "g7-guidance.json:review.g7-sec-policy.how"
msgid "Give the route for reporting a vulnerability in this model and who answers it. A published model needs a contact that outlives the person who trained it."
msgstr ""

#: g7-guidance.json
msgctxt "g7-guidance.json:review.g7-kpi-security.how"
msgid "Record what you measured on the security side — adversarial or jailbreak testing, refusal rates, red-team results — with the method and the date. If nothing was measured, say so plainly."
msgstr ""
